1. Create an instance of the AEAD GCM cipher class.
2. Set the encryption and decryption keys.
3. Initialize the cipher with the desired mode (e.g., CBC, CTR).
4. Call the `updateAAD` method to authenticate the data before encrypting or decrypting it.
5. Encrypt or decrypt the data using the cipher.

Here's some sample code demonstrating how to use the `updateAAD` method:
```java
import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.IvParameterSpec;

public class AeadGcmAuthentication {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Generate a secret key
        KeyGenerator keyGenerator = KeyGenerator.getInstance("AES");
        keyGenerator.init(256);
        SecretKey secretKey = keyGenerator.generateKey();

        // Create an instance of the AEAD GCM cipher class
        Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");

        // Set the encryption and decryption keys
        cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, secretKey);

        // Initialize the cipher with the desired mode (e.g., CBC, CTR)
        IvParameterSpec ivParameterSpec = new IvParameterSpec("0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567".getBytes());
        cipher.init(ivParameterSpec);

        // Authenticate the data before encrypting or decrypting it
        byte[] data = "This is some data to be encrypted or decrypted.".getBytes();
        cipher.updateAAD(data);

        // Encrypt the data
        byte[] encryptedData = cipher.doFinal(data);

        // Decrypt the data
