To get the user's session using the jsSDK, you can follow these steps:

1. Include the jsSDK script in your HTML file:
```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/js-sdk@2.14.3/dist/js-sdk.min.js"></script>
```
1. Create a JavaScript file (e.g., `get_user_session.js`) and add the following code:
```javascript
// Initialize the jsSDK
const sdk = new JSWebSocket('wss://your-server-url/ws');

// Connect to the server
sdk.connect();

// Listen for the 'open' event
sdk.on('open', () => {
  // Send a message to the server to request the user's session
  sdk.send({
    type: 'request_session',
  });
});

// Listen for the 'message' event
sdk.on('message', (event) => {
  // Check if the message contains the user's session
  const session = event.data.session;
  if (session) {
    // Store the session in a local storage or session storage
    localStorage.setItem('session', session);
  }
});
```
Replace `'your-server-url'` with the URL of your server. This script will connect to the server, send a message to request the user's session, and listen for the server's response. If the server sends the user's session, it will be stored in the local storage or session storage.

2. Call the `get_user_session.js` script from your HTML file:
```html
<script src="get_user_session.js"></script>
```
This will initialize the jsSDK and retrieve the user's session. You can then use the stored session in your application.

Note: This example assumes that your server is set up to handle the `request_session` message and send the user's session back to the client. You may need to modify your server's code to support this feature.

Here's the `redis.js` file with the requested class and instance:

```javascript
const { Redis } = require("ioredis");

class RedisClient {
  constructor() {
    this.client = new Redis();
    this.client.on("error", (err) => {
      console.error(`Redis error: ${err}`);
    });
  }

  async isAlive() {
    try {
      await this.client.ping();
      return true;
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`Error checking Redis connection: ${error}`);
      return false;
    }
  }

  async get(key) {
    const value = await this.client.get(key);
    if (value === null) {
      throw new Error(`Key ${key} not found in Redis`);
    }
    return value;
  }

  async set(key, value, duration) {
    await this.client.setex(key, duration, value);
  }

  async del(key) {
    await this.client.del(key);
  }
}

const redisClient = new RedisClient();

module.exports = redisClient;
```

