To add custom CSS to a Shopify section and make the image smaller if the section classname is "feature-row__image lazyautosizes ls-is-cached lazyloaded", you can follow these steps:

1. Create a new custom CSS file in your theme's `assets/css` folder, e.g., `custom-section-styles.css`.
2. Add the following CSS code to the file:
```css
.feature-row__image.lazyautosizes.ls-is-cached.lazyloaded {
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}
```
This CSS code will target the `.feature-row__image` element with the specified class names and set its width to 100% and height to auto, making the image smaller.
3. In your theme's `theme.liquid` file, add the following code to include the custom CSS file:
```liquid
{% include 'custom-section-styles' %}
```
4. Save both files and refresh your Shopify store to see the changes.

Note that this solution assumes that the `.feature-row__image` element has the specified class names. If the class names are different, you'll need to adjust the CSS selector accordingly.
